'''Godavari Biorefineries Limited''', formerly '''The Godavari Sugar Mills Ltd''', is an Indian company which operates two [[sugar refinery|sugar refineries]] and manufactures more than 20 products from [[renewable resources]].

== History ==
On Oct 2024, the company have raised {{INRConvert|166|c|year=2024}} from anchor investors, one day ahead of the IPO.<ref>{{Cite news |last=Sethi |first=Vaamanaa |date=22 Oct 2024 |title=Godavari Biorefineries IPO: Chemicals producer garners ₹166 crore from anchor investors ahead of IPO |url=https://www.livemint.com/market/ipo/godavari-biorefineries-ipo-chemical-producer-garners-166-crore-from-anchor-investors-ahead-of-ipo-11729614456604.html |access-date=19 Jun 2025 |work=Live Mint}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |last=Thayil |first=Pratiksha |date=2024-10-22 |title=Godavari Biorefineries Raises Rs 166 Crore From Anchor Investors Ahead Of IPO |url=https://www.ndtvprofit.com/ipos/godavari-biorefineries-ipo-anchor-investors-funding |access-date=2025-06-19 |website=NDTV Profit |language=en}}</ref> The company opened its [[initial public offering]] (IPO) in 23 Oct 2024 with total size of ₹555 crore.<ref>{{cite news |last1=Podishetti |first1=Akash |title=Godavari Biorefineries shares list at 12.5% discount over IPO price |url=https://economictimes.indiatimes.com/markets/stocks/news/godavari-biorefineries-shares-to-debut-today-gmp-hints-at-flat-listing/articleshow/114755799.cms |access-date=19 November 2024 |work=The Economic Times |date=30 October 2024}}</ref> The offering consists of a fresh issue of equity shares worth ₹325 crore and an Offer-for-Sale (OFS) of 65.27 lakh shares valued at ₹230 crore by promoters and an investor.<ref>{{Cite web |date=2024-10-30 |title=Godavari Biorefineries shares make poor start on bourses; list at nearly 13% discount - CNBC TV18 |url=https://www.cnbctv18.com/market/godavari-biorefineries-ipo-listing-today-share-price-makes-poor-start-on-bourses-list-at-discount-19501292.htm |access-date=2025-06-21 |website=CNBCTV18 |language=en}}</ref>

In December 2024, the company has signed an international licence agreement with US based company [[Catalyxx Inc.]], to get the exclusive rights in utilising advanced technology for converting ethanol into biobutanol and other higher alcohols.<ref>{{Cite web |date=2024-12-02 |title=Godavari Biorefineries signs pact with Catalyxx to enhance ethanol - CNBC TV18 |url=https://www.cnbctv18.com/market/stocks/godavari-biorefineries-share-price-pact-with-catalyxx-to-enhance-ethanol-into-biobutanol-higher-alcohol-19518286.htm |access-date=2025-06-19 |website=CNBCTV18 |language=en}}</ref>

On Jan 2025, according to the [[Securities and Exchange Board of India|SEBI]] Regulations, the company has received {{INRConvert|93|c|year=2025}} as the Demand Notice received for Non-Payment of [[Goods and Services Tax (India)|Goods and Service Tax]] (GST) on clearance of [[Extra Neutral Alcohol]] (ENA) for the period from Jul 2017 to Mar 2021. The Authority demand ₹46.84 crore as non-payment of GST and ₹ 46.84 as penalty.<ref>{{Cite web |last= |title=Godavari Biorefineries faces ₹93 cr GST demand - ET LegalWorld |url=https://legal.economictimes.indiatimes.com/news/corporate-business/godavari-biorefineries-faces-93-cr-gst-demand/116965183 |access-date=2025-06-19 |website=ETLegalWorld.com |language=en}}</ref>

